Raw triangles keep their proportions in an expanded aspect ratio
(warecomp STATUS.md round 23).

RDP / raw triangles are in the colour image's pixels, but the framebuffer
renderer mapped them across the whole wide target: in 16:9 they were
stretched by 4/3 about the centre. S2DEX matrix sprites are drawn as raw
triangles (0030), so Worms Armageddon's turning sprites (the air strike's
target, shells, flying worms) looked squashed and leaned as they turned,
and sat off their place towards the sides. They're now scaled like rects:
by the original width over the wide width, about the centre.

--- a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
@@ -1672,6 +1672,12 @@
                         case Projection::Type::Triangle: {
                             instanceDrawCall.type = InstanceDrawCall::Type::RawTriangles;
                             triangles.indexStart = call.meshDesc.rawVertexStart;
+
+                            // Raw triangles are in the colour image's pixels: in an expanded aspect ratio, keep them
+                            // in proportion and in the centred original area like rects, rather than stretched
+                            // across the wide target (S2DEX matrix sprites, which are drawn as raw triangles,
+                            // looked squashed as they turned).
+                            triangles.screenScale.x = originalWidth / wideWidth;
                             break;
                         }
                         case Projection::Type::None:
